  "selection_rule": "Use the cheapest fit-for-purpose capability that preserves evidence quality. Prefer primary/authoritative sources over search-engine summaries. GitHub-connected workers that cannot invoke repository scripts directly MUST use the repo-runner bridge before declaring an otherwise healthy provider unavailable.",
  "fallback_rule": "If a preferred provider is unavailable, rate-limited, quota-exhausted or lacks credentials, record the reason and use the next suitable capability without silently weakening provenance. Current practical fallbacks: Semantic Scholar -> OpenAlex/arXiv/Crossref; E2B -> Judge0/local sandbox; Piston -> Judge0/local sandbox; Tavily/Exa -> DDGS/native web; Groq 8B small-model proxy -> true target/local 4B when available, otherwise Hugging Face/other model provider under normal quota policy; Groq 8B small-model proxy -> true target/local 4B when available, otherwise Hugging Face/other model provider under normal quota policy; Groq 8B small-model proxy -> true target/local 4B when available, otherwise Hugging Face/other model provider under normal quota policy; Groq 8B small-model proxy -> true target/local 4B when available, otherwise Hugging Face/other model provider under normal quota policy.",
  "verification_rule": "Mark a capability RUNTIME_VERIFIED only after an actual successful provider call; credential presence alone is not verification. Preserve transient degradation separately from credential validity.",
  "small_model_proxy_policy": "research_entity/global/SMALL_MODEL_PROXY_POLICY.md"
